# Trust-root paths: lane config, grants and rules, the workflows and actions lanes run
# from the default branch, and the plugins lanes load. Code-owner review is off by owner
# decision, so an owner here is only requested for review. A write lane is not asked to fix a
# path listed here, but its token can change any file; the PR is the review step
# (docs/conventions/pr-pipeline/README.md#trust-root-paths).

/docs/conventions/pr-pipeline.yaml @kyle-sexton
/docs/conventions/pr-pipeline/** @kyle-sexton
/.github/actions/** @kyle-sexton
/.github/standards/** @kyle-sexton
# Standards-synced data files outside .github/workflows/ have no owner (an entry with no owner
# unowns the path, and the last match wins), so a standards-sync pull request touching only these
# requests no review. runner-policy.mjs and the trusted-actors files stay owned above.
/.github/standards/github-actions-conventions/vocabulary.json
/.github/standards/github-actions-conventions/vocabulary.schema.json
/.github/standards/pyright/pyrightconfig.json
/.github/standards/runner-policy/package-lock.json
/.github/standards/runner-policy/package.json
/.github/standards/runner-policy/policy.json
/.github/standards/runner-policy/policy.schema.json
/.github/standards/runner-policy/repository-policy.schema.json
/.github/workflows/** @kyle-sexton
# These synced caller workflows come from standards: edits are blocked by the required
# check-managed-files job and deletions since ci-workflows v0.39.4, so they need no owner.
/.github/workflows/pr-check-managed-files-hosted.yml
/.github/workflows/pr-review-hosted.yml
/.github/workflows/pr-review-security-hosted.yml
/.github/scripts/** @kyle-sexton
/.github/CODEOWNERS @kyle-sexton
/.claude-plugin/marketplace.json @kyle-sexton
/plugins/code-tidying/** @kyle-sexton
/plugins/ai-slop/** @kyle-sexton
/plugins/review/** @kyle-sexton
/plugins/source-control/** @kyle-sexton
